211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Introduction  Facial emotion recognition \(FER\) represents a crucial component of affective computing and human-computer interaction systems. The ability to automatically detect and classify human emotions from facial expressions has wide-ranging applications across various domains, including psychology, healthcare, marketing, security, education, and entertainment. This report analyzes a Convolutional Neural Network \(CNN\) model developed for recognizing seven basic facial emotions: anger, disgust, fear, happiness, neutral, sadness, and surprise. Background and Significance Human facial expressions communicate a wealth of information about emotional states, intentions, and reactions. While humans can intuitively recognize emotions displayed on faces, developing automated systems that can perform this task with comparable accuracy presents significant technical challenges. Recent advances in deep learning, particularly CNNs, have revolutionized computer vision tasks including facial emotion recognition. Research Objectives This project aims to develop and evaluate a CNN-based system for accurately classifying facial emotions across seven categories. The specific objectives include:)
/E (Introduction  Facial emotion recognition \(FER\) represents a crucial component of affective computing and human-computer interaction systems. The ability to automatically detect and classify human emotions from facial expressions has wide-ranging applications across various domains, including psychology, healthcare, marketing, security, education, and entertainment. This report analyzes a Convolutional Neural Network \(CNN\) model developed for recognizing seven basic facial emotions: anger, disgust, fear, happiness, neutral, sadness, and surprise. Background and Significance Human facial expressions communicate a wealth of information about emotional states, intentions, and reactions. While humans can intuitively recognize emotions displayed on faces, developing automated systems that can perform this task with comparable accuracy presents significant technical challenges. Recent advances in deep learning, particularly CNNs, have revolutionized computer vision tasks including facial emotion recognition. Research Objectives This project aims to develop and evaluate a CNN-based system for accurately classifying facial emotions across seven categories. The specific objectives include:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
