230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The field of facial emotion recognition is grounded in psychological theories of emotion. Paul Ekman's pioneering work established the concept of six universal basic emotions \(anger, disgust, fear, happiness, sadness, and surprise\) that are recognized across cultures, with neutral later added as a seventh category. This categorical approach to emotions forms the foundation of most facial emotion recognition systems. Alternative frameworks include dimensional models \(valence-arousal space\) and the Facial Action Coding System \(FACS\), which breaks down facial expressions into individual muscle movements called Action Units \(AUs\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
