/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The earliest automated facial emotion recognition systems emerged in the 1990s, utilizing geometric feature-based methods that tracked key facial points and measured their movements. Kobayashi and Hara \(1997\) developed one of the first systems using a neural network trained on displacement vectors of facial feature points. During the 2000s, appearance-based methods gained popularity, with Bartlett et al. \(2003\) using Gabor filters and Support Vector Machines to classify facial expressions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [33]
>>
