372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Conclusion The facial emotion recognition CNN model demonstrates promising results for certain emotions \(happiness, surprise\) while facing challenges with others \(fear, sadness, anger, disgust\). The overall accuracy of 54.45% indicates room for significant improvement, particularly in distinguishing between similar negative emotions. By addressing class imbalance, enhancing the model architecture, implementing advanced training strategies, and expanding the dataset, future iterations of this system could achieve substantially better performance across all emotion categories. The deployment as a web application makes this technology accessible and demonstrates its potential for real-world applications in fields such as human-computer interaction, mental health assessment, market research, and educational technology.)
/E (Conclusion The facial emotion recognition CNN model demonstrates promising results for certain emotions \(happiness, surprise\) while facing challenges with others \(fear, sadness, anger, disgust\). The overall accuracy of 54.45% indicates room for significant improvement, particularly in distinguishing between similar negative emotions. By addressing class imbalance, enhancing the model architecture, implementing advanced training strategies, and expanding the dataset, future iterations of this system could achieve substantially better performance across all emotion categories. The deployment as a web application makes this technology accessible and demonstrates its potential for real-world applications in fields such as human-computer interaction, mental health assessment, market research, and educational technology.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
